#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:3
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:5
msgid ""
"This tutorial covers the core pipx workflow: install an application, run it, "
"upgrade it, and remove it. Work through it top to bottom with one small "
"package, and you will know the commands you need day to day."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:10
msgid "Install pipx first. See :doc:`Install pipx <../how-to/install-pipx>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:14
msgid "Packages and apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:16
msgid ""
"pipx installs **packages** and exposes their **apps**. A package is what you "
"download from `PyPI <https://pypi.org>`_, such as ``pycowsay`` or "
"``httpie``. An app is a command that package puts on your ``PATH`` through a "
"`console script entry point <https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/"
"specifications/entry-points/>`_. One package can expose several apps: "
"``httpie`` gives you ``http``, ``httpie``, and ``https``. For the full "
"picture, see :doc:`How pipx works <../explanation/how-pipx-works>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:24
msgid "The lifecycle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:39
msgid "Install your first app"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:41
msgid "Pick a small package to try. ``pycowsay`` works well:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:43
msgid ""
"$ pipx install pycowsay\n"
"  installed package pycowsay 0.0.0.2, installed using Python 3.12.3\n"
"  These apps are now available\n"
"    - pycowsay\n"
"  These manual pages are now available\n"
"    - man6/pycowsay.6\n"
"done! ✨ 🌟 ✨"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:53
msgid ""
"pipx creates an isolated virtual environment for ``pycowsay``, installs it "
"there, and links the ``pycowsay`` command into a directory on your ``PATH``, "
"without ``sudo``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:57
msgid "Confirm it worked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:59
msgid "Run the app from any directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:61
msgid ""
"$ pycowsay moo\n"
"  ---\n"
"< moo >\n"
"  ---\n"
"   \\   ^__^\n"
"    \\  (oo)\\_______\n"
"       (__)\\       )\\/\\\n"
"           ||----w |\n"
"           ||     ||"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:73
msgid "If you see the cow, pipx is working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:77
msgid ""
"``pycowsay: command not found``? pipx installed the app but its directory is "
"not on your ``PATH`` yet. Run ``pipx ensurepath``, then open a new terminal. "
"See :doc:`Install pipx <../how-to/install-pipx>` and :doc:`Troubleshoot <../"
"how-to/troubleshoot>` if it persists."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:83
msgid "List installed apps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:85
msgid ""
"$ pipx list\n"
"venvs are in /home/user/.local/share/pipx/venvs\n"
"apps are exposed on your $PATH at /home/user/.local/bin\n"
"manual pages are exposed at /home/user/.local/share/man\n"
"shell completions are exposed at /home/user/.local/share\n"
"   package pycowsay 0.0.0.2, installed using Python 3.12.3\n"
"    - pycowsay\n"
"    - man6/pycowsay.6"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:96
msgid ""
"The output shows each virtual environment's location, the apps it exposes, "
"and the Python version it uses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:100
msgid "Run an app without installing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:102
msgid ""
"``pipx run`` executes an app from a cached temporary environment without "
"installing it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:104
msgid "$ pipx run pycowsay moo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:108
msgid ""
"Reach for this when you want to try a tool once. The :doc:`run-applications` "
"tutorial covers it in depth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:112
msgid "Upgrade an app"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:114
msgid "Upgrade a single app to its latest release:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:116
msgid "$ pipx upgrade pycowsay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:120
msgid "Or upgrade everything at once:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:122
msgid "$ pipx upgrade-all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:128
msgid ""
"See what has an update before upgrading with ``pipx list --outdated``. The "
"output lists each package's installed and available versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:133
msgid "Uninstall an app"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:135
msgid "$ pipx uninstall pycowsay"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorial/getting-started.rst:139
msgid ""
"pipx deletes the isolated environment and removes the command from your "
"``PATH``, leaving nothing behind."
msgstr ""

